+# Flutter Post Actions Patch
+
+This patch adds three files you can apply inside the `inzone-flutter-app` repository to add Edit/Delete actions to posts:
+
+- `lib/services/api_client.dart` — small API client with `getPostForEdit` and `deletePost` methods.
+- `lib/widgets/post_actions_menu.dart` — `PostActionsMenu` widget that shows Edit/Delete for post owners.
+- `README_POST_ACTIONS_PATCH.md` — this file with apply instructions.
+
+How to apply
+1. Copy `flutter-post-actions.patch` into the root of your `inzone-flutter-app` repo (or run `curl` to fetch it there).
+2. From the root of `inzone-flutter-app`, run:
+
+```bash
+git apply /path/to/flutter-post-actions.patch
+```
+
+or if you placed the patch file in the repo root:
+
+```bash
+git apply flutter-post-actions.patch
+```
+
+3. Verify the files are added:
+
+```bash
+git status --porcelain
+```
+
+4. Add the files and commit:
+
+```bash
+git add lib/services/api_client.dart lib/widgets/post_actions_menu.dart README_POST_ACTIONS_PATCH.md
+git commit -m "feat: add post actions menu and api client helpers for edit/delete"
+```
+
+5. Update your routing to register the named route `/createPost` (or adjust the widget's push to your existing route name). Ensure `CreatePostPage` reads `ModalRoute.of(context)!.settings.arguments` or accepts the `initialPost` via constructor.
+
+Notes
+- Update `ApiClient(baseUrl: ...)` with your backend URL (use `http://10.0.2.2:<port>` for Android emulator).
+- If you use Firebase auth, pass the user's ID token to `ApiClient` methods to enable server-side verification.
+- The `CreatePostPage` must support prefilling fields and updating an existing post; the patch only navigates and supplies the post JSON as the route `arguments`.
+
+If you want, I can instead produce a patch that modifies existing files (e.g., injects the `PostActionsMenu` into your `PostCard` widget) — for that I will need the exact `PostCard` file path from the Flutter repo.
+
+-- End
+